{"description":"Audit an ALREADY-redacted PDF and report whether sensitive text still survives underneath the redaction \u2014 the 'did my black boxes actually remove the data?' check. Most tools redact by drawing a rectangle over text while leaving the characters in the file, where they stay selectable and extractable. This re-extracts the text on-device and flags any emails, SSNs, phone or card numbers that are still present, each with a MASKED preview \u2014 the raw value never leaves the machine. It checks the page text layer, text surviving UNDER redaction marks, incremental-update prior revisions (the classic 'redacted then saved, original still in the file' failure), document metadata, AcroForm field values and embedded attachments, and returns a coverage report so a clean result is scoped to what was inspected. A non-empty result means the redaction leaked. Nothing is uploaded. (Pattern-based: names/addresses, image-only text, and the surfaces listed as not-inspected aren't covered; absence of hits isn't proof of completeness.) Free tier (no native engine): reports are EVALUATION-marked \u2014 for evaluation, not production reliance \u2014 and limited (by default) to 10 attempts a month, shared with find_sensitive_regions and counted locally; past the cap this tool returns a structured 'free-cap' refusal. A configured native engine is not capped. `scanComplete` is false when some page or stream could not be read; then `clean` only means nothing was found in what WAS read (possibly nothing) and the text leads with an INCOMPLETE SCAN warning \u2014 never report such a result as clean. The result also carries `verdict`: the same presented-document check the Omitly desktop app's 'Check any PDF' runs, as one of three verdicts about THE CHECK \u2014 'safe_to_send' (every check that applies to this file passed, within what the check covers; `verdict.result.notChecked` lists what it did not), 'needs_review' (something needs a person to look before sending; `blocking` true means a problem such as recoverable text under a box was found), or 'cannot_verify' (the check could not complete, so no verdict is given). The verdict covers hidden, covered and recoverable content (text under boxes, metadata, layers, attachments, earlier versions, comments, alternate text); it does not judge whether VISIBLE text should be there \u2014 the pattern findings above do \u2014 so a visible identifier can be a finding while the verdict is 'safe_to_send'. None of the verdicts is a statement that the document is safe. The full audit v2 report behind the verdict is not returned here; it is available from the engine's `check` command (`omitly-redact`) and the desktop app.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","properties":{"pdfPath":{"description":"absolute path to the supposedly-redacted PDF to audit","type":"string"}},"required":["pdfPath"],"type":"object"},"name":"check_redaction","outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"byKind":{"additionalProperties":{"maximum":9007199254740991,"minimum":-9007199254740991,"type":"integer"},"propertyNames":{"type":"string"},"type":"object"},"clean":{"type":"boolean"},"coverage":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"acroformScanned":{"type":"boolean"},"annotationAppearancesScanned":{"maximum":9007199254740991,"minimum":-9007199254740991,"type":"integer"},"attachmentsScanned":{"type":"boolean"},"formXobjectsScanned":{"maximum":9007199254740991,"minimum":-9007199254740991,"type":"integer"},"metadataScanned":{"type":"boolean"},"notScanned":{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"pagesFailedCount":{"maximum":9007199254740991,"minimum":-9007199254740991,"type":"integer"},"pagesScanned":{"anyOf":[{"maximum":9007199254740991,"minimum":-9007199254740991,"type":"integer"},{"type":"null"}]},"pagesTotal":{"anyOf":[{"maximum":9007199254740991,"minimum":-9007199254740991,"type":"integer"},{"type":"null"}]},"priorRevisionsScanned":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["pagesScanned","pagesTotal","notScanned","priorRevisionsScanned","metadataScanned","acroformScanned","attachmentsScanned","formXobjectsScanned","annotationAppearancesScanned","pagesFailedCount"],"type":"object"},"evaluation":{"const":true,"type":"boolean"},"offPage":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"kind":{"type":"string"},"preview":{"type":"string"},"source":{"type":"string"}},"required":["source","kind","preview"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"regions":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"height":{"type":"number"},"kind":{"type":"string"},"page":{"maximum":9007199254740991,"minimum":-9007199254740991,"type":"integer"},"preview":{"type":"string"},"width":{"type":"number"},"x":{"type":"number"},"y":{"type":"number"}},"required":["page","x","y","width","height","kind","preview"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"scanComplete":{"type":"boolean"},"survivors":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"height":{"type":"number"},"kind":{"type":"string"},"page":{"maximum":9007199254740991,"minimum":-9007199254740991,"type":"integer"},"preview":{"type":"string"},"width":{"type":"number"},"x":{"type":"number"},"y":{"type":"number"}},"required":["page","x","y","width","height","kind","preview"],"type":"object"},"type":"array"},"totalFindings":{"maximum":9007199254740991,"minimum":0,"type":"integer"},"verdict":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"blocking":{"type":"boolean"},"reason_code":{"anyOf":[{"enum":["input_too_large","check_failed","check_unavailable","result_invalid"],"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"result":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"blocking":{"type":"boolean"},"checked":{"items":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"pages":{"items":{"maximum":1000000,"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"maxItems":10000,"type":"array"},"text":{"maxLength":1024,"pattern":"^[^\\u0000-\\u001f\\u007f-\\u009f\\u20